{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/124096-sell-me-on-demon","id":124096,"title":"Sell Me On Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-02T16:15:56-07:00","id":124096,"title":"Sell Me On Demon","content":"So with the revelation that <i>Hunter: Mortal Remains</i> has a group that can <b>PUNCH THE COVERS OFF DEMONS</b>, I am taking a second look at the newest splat to grace the WoD family. I rather enjoy the strange and esoteric themes WoD has come up with so far, and for that to be codified into a technognostic splat? Very, very interesting, but I'm not totally convinced it's worth my while. Any opinions, thoughts and the like on the game that might change my mind are appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:33:48-07:00","id":124112,"title":"","content":"Could you let me know about your hang ups? Once I'm done with this test, I'll tell you how Demon became my second favorite game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:58:30-07:00","id":124126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/124096-sell-me-on-demon?p=124112#post124112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you let me know about your hang ups? Once I'm done with this test, I'll tell you how Demon became my second favorite game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though I do love the esoteric setting it provides, a lot of fantasy/sci-fi/horror/etc. I've been perusing lately has lost my immersion. There's a point where, no matter how well it's written, the grimdark or the awesome factor or whatever else is there piles up to the point where it feels too fantastic. I'm looking for something that will constantly have me questioning, constantly throwing curveballs at me that let me sink my teeth in. An example of where I struggle with one of my games is Werewolf; it's an amazing feeling with a starter character where you feel so dwarfed and insignificant, even though you have spiritual powers, and that you're constantly at odds and lost in this great, spiritual hellscape. Then you get enough power, and...armour-wearing werewolves wielding dual-fireswords while smashing up things in a Neanderthal-ish form. It turns almost comic book-ish.<br /> <br /> Yeah. Looking to avoid something like that, if that makes sense \u2014 something that keeps the mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:41:30-07:00","id":124152,"title":"","content":"It's a game about rogue spies on the run from an ever-present foe, hiding within the nooks and crannies where reality doesn't fit together nicely. It's a game where your powers are taking the secret laws of the universe and slipping through the loopholes. It's a game with the most clever look at demonic bargains I've ever seen. It has a pervasive weirdness about it that many of the other nWoD games lack, you can tie in almost any internet rumor or weird conspiracy theory as a plot hook, and the big question of the God-Machine is wholly up to the Storyteller to answer (if they even choose to!). You're free to make any character concept under the sun. It's tense. It's unique. It's New Weird meets classic espionage thriller meets the World of Darkness we all love and fear. Gove it a shot; it's my favorite nWoD line by far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:09:18-07:00","id":124170,"title":"","content":"I find that the blend of technology/computers/physics with the espionage itself is fun, but really, the overlay of it all with the context of angels and demons is delicious. despite being fallen subdivinity programs, they're also very assuredly demons. Our demons have had talks on the nature of God, of Hell, and of morality. You can use the game to make regular demons--Ive got npcs including an incubus, a possessor/Fallen (film) style demon, a big brawling engine of hellfire and blasphemy. But the added mechanical elements gives these demons a unique edge that sets them apart from other monsters. Demons can be evil, but they dont do so like hungry addicts (vamps), cackling lunatics (changeling), or even dark religious fervor (mummy). what makes demons so evil is how dispassionately and pragmatically they sin. they don't enjoy it, but it must be done. The rather emotionless behavior of angels (and even demons during &quot;business talks&quot;) is a unique sort of horror. More Terminator and Dark City, but with bits of Salem and Supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}